# Line endings.
#
# Without this, each machine's core.autocrlf decides, and Prisma migration
# checksums are computed over the file BYTES. A migration baselined from a
# Windows checkout (CRLF) records a different checksum than the same file
# checked out on a Linux CI runner or deploy host (LF), and `prisma migrate
# deploy` then refuses with "the migration was modified after it was applied".
#
# That is not hypothetical here: the 0_init baseline was first recorded with a
# CRLF checksum from a Windows machine, which would have failed the very next
# Render deploy.
#
# Migration SQL is the case that actually breaks, but pinning the whole tree to
# LF keeps checksums, diffs and shell scripts consistent everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these — mangling bytes corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.keystore binary
*.jar binary
